// What the pool does not yet do right, because the compiler does not. No
// finalizing gap is left to pin: a value assigned over through '&mut pool[r]'
// is finalized as it is replaced (finalize.cone).
//
// THE HOLE, which compiles today and dangles, so no check here can pin what
// it prints. Written out so a reader knows what is not yet safe:
//
//   fn frozen(p &mut Pool[Pt], q &mut Pool[Pt]) i64 {
//     imm r = p.add(new Pt(1, 2));
//     imm x = &mut p[r];
//     q.remove(r);               // called with one pool twice: through a
//                                // '&mut' parameter the pool is reached by a
//     x.x;                       // shared path, which a borrow does not
//   }                            // freeze, so x reads a finalized value
//
// It is freezing through a shared path. A borrow from 'pool[r]' or
// '&mut pool[r]', or an Option from 'get' or 'getMut', held in a local
// freezes a local pool: 'remove', an 'add'
// (which may move every value), and moving or dropping it are refused while
// the borrow is live. A pool reached through a '&mut Pool' parameter, a field
// of 'self' or a 'Rc[mut, T]' owner is not frozen, since another reference may
// reach it; Jon's rule refuses such a borrow, and waits on 'uni' reborrowing.
// A static pool (a module's global) changed by a function called while a
// borrow of it lives is not seen.
//
// No longer a hole: a borrow from a pool, bare or inside the Option 'get' and
// 'getMut' return, carries the pool's loan wherever it goes. Returning the
// Option from the function holding the pool, storing it through a parameter,
// and matching the borrow out of it and returning that are refused, as
// returning or storing away a bare 'pool[r]' is; kept in an outer variable
// and used after the pool ends, any of them is refused too. The compiler's
// suite pins each route (test/cases/region/region_flow_pool_escape.cone).
//
//   fn escapes() Option[&Pt] {
//     mut p = Pool[Pt].empty();
//     imm r = p.add(new Pt(1, 2));
//     p.get(r);                  // refused: the pool dies here, and the
//   }                            // borrow in the Option would be returned
//
// Held in a variable of the function and used while the pool lives, any of
// these borrows is fine.

mod gaps;

import testing use *;
import pool use *;

fn main() i32 {
  done();
}
